    "explanation": "`ApplicationContext` is the central, most advanced interface representing the Spring IoC container. \nIt extends the basic `BeanFactory` interface and adds powerful enterprise-specific features, such as:\n1. Eager instantiation of Singleton beans (they are created on startup, surfacing errors immediately).\n2. AOP integration.\n3. Internationalization (i18n) message resolution.\n4. Event publishing (ApplicationEventPublisher).\n5. Web application support (`WebApplicationContext`).",
    "example": "If you need to publish an event that a new user registered so an email listener can catch it, you use the ApplicationContext to publish it.",
