    "tip": "By default, every Spring Bean is a Singleton. There is only one instance of that object in the entire JVM memory.",
    "mistake": "Thinking a Spring Bean must implement Serializable or follow the old JavaBeans specification (getters/setters). It doesn't. It's just a managed object.",
