    "category": "3. Spring Bean Lifecycle & Configuration",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "`@PostConstruct` is an annotation applied to a method that needs to be executed **immediately after dependency injection is complete**.\nBecause dependencies are not fully injected while the constructor is running, you cannot rely on them in the constructor. `@PostConstruct` guarantees that all `@Autowired` dependencies are completely wired and the bean is fully ready for setup tasks.",
