    "explanation": "Externalized configuration is the practice of keeping configuration variables (like database URLs, passwords, API keys, port numbers) outside of your compiled Java code. \nSpring allows you to read these values from properties files (`application.properties`), YAML files, environment variables, or command-line arguments. This allows you to run the exact same compiled `.jar` file in Development, QA, and Production just by changing the external configuration.",
