    "explanation": "Both are used to read externalized configuration, but they scale differently:\n- **`@Value`:** Used to inject a **single property** directly into a field. It is quick but doesn't support structured data or validation well.\n- **`@ConfigurationProperties`:** Used to map an **entire hierarchical group of properties** (e.g., all `mail.smtp.*` properties) into a dedicated, strongly-typed POJO. It supports nested objects, lists, and JSR-303 validation (e.g., `@NotNull`).",
