    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Prior to Spring Boot, traditional Spring development suffered from massive configuration overhead. \nDevelopers had to write extensive XML files (beans.xml, web.xml), manually manage complex dependency version collisions in Maven, and install, configure, and deploy WAR files to external application servers (like Tomcat or WebSphere).\nSpring Boot was introduced to eliminate this \"boilerplate\" configuration, embrace convention over configuration, and allow developers to deploy apps as simple, self-contained executable JAR files (fat JARs).",
