    "explanation": "Auto-Configuration is the \"magic\" behind Spring Boot.\nIt is an intelligent mechanism that inspects your classpath, sees which JARs you have imported, and automatically configures the necessary Spring Beans based on sensible defaults.\nIt uses the `@Conditional` annotations heavily. For example, if it sees `spring-webmvc` on the classpath, it says: \"You must be building a web app. I will automatically configure a DispatcherServlet, an embedded Tomcat, and JSON converters for you.\"",
