    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Traditionally, Java web apps were packaged as `.war` files and manually deployed into external, pre-installed web servers (like Tomcat or WebSphere). \nSpring Boot changes this paradigm by embedding the server directly inside your compiled Java application. When you run `java -jar myapp.jar`, the application starts up, unpacks the embedded server into memory, and hosts itself. You don't need to install anything on the host machine other than Java.",
