    "category": "7. Spring Data JPA / Hibernate",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "`@Id` is a JPA annotation used to define the Primary Key field of an Entity. \nEvery single JPA Entity is absolutely required to have exactly one field (or a composite key) marked with `@Id`. This is how Hibernate uniquely identifies every object in its persistence context and maps it to a unique row in the database.",
