    "category": "7. Spring Data JPA / Hibernate",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "`@GeneratedValue` is paired with `@Id`. It tells Hibernate: \"Do not expect me to manually provide an ID for this object before saving it. Let the database (or Hibernate) automatically generate a unique ID for me.\"",
    "example": "If you create a new `User` in Java, its ID is `null`. When you call `repository.save(user)`, Hibernate intercepts the call, asks the database to generate an ID, and injects that ID into your Java object.",
