    "title": "What is pagination in Spring Data JPA?",
    "category": "7. Spring Data JPA / Hibernate",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Pagination is the process of retrieving a massive dataset in small, manageable chunks (pages) rather than loading everything into memory at once.\nSpring Data JPA makes this incredibly easy via the `Pageable` interface. You pass a `PageRequest` (containing page number and size) to a repository method. Spring automatically generates the underlying SQL limits (e.g., `LIMIT 10 OFFSET 20`), executes a count query to find total records, and returns a `Page` object.",
