    "id": 119,
    "title": "How can you solve the N+1 problem?",
    "category": "7. Spring Data JPA / Hibernate",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "There are three primary ways to solve the N+1 problem in Spring Data JPA:\n1. **`JOIN FETCH` in JPQL:** The most common. You write a custom query that explicitly tells Hibernate to use a SQL JOIN to pull the parent and children in a single query.\n2. **`@EntityGraph`:** A Spring Data annotation that allows you to dynamically override a LAZY fetch to EAGER for a specific repository method.\n3. **Hibernate `@BatchSize`:** Tells Hibernate to fetch children in batches (e.g., IN clauses of 50 IDs at a time) rather than 1 by 1. Doesn't reduce to 1 query, but reduces N queries to N/50.",
    "example": "Instead of letting Hibernate lazy load the books later, force it to fetch the authors AND their books right now.",
