    "explanation": "Entity relationships map the Object-Oriented concept of object associations (Class A has a reference to Class B) to the Relational Database concept of Foreign Keys.\nJPA defines four types of associations:\n1. **`@OneToOne`:** A User has exactly one Profile.\n2. **`@OneToMany`:** A Department has many Employees.\n3. **`@ManyToOne`:** Many Employees belong to one Department. (This is the most common, as it maps directly to a standard Foreign Key column).\n4. **`@ManyToMany`:** Many Students attend Many Courses (Requires a hidden \"join table\" in the database to map).",
