    "id": 137,
    "title": "How would you identify service boundaries?",
    "category": "9. Microservices",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Identifying service boundaries is the hardest part of microservices. \nThe industry standard approach is **Domain-Driven Design (DDD)**, specifically using the concept of **Bounded Contexts**.\nYou group features based on business capabilities rather than technical layers. A Bounded Context is a linguistic and functional boundary. For example, a \"Product\" means something entirely different to the Billing department (price, tax code) than it does to the Shipping department (weight, dimensions). Therefore, Billing and Shipping should be separate services.",
    "example": "Bad boundaries: A UI service, a Business Logic service, and a Database service. Good boundaries: An Order service, a User service, and an Inventory service.",
