    "title": "What is service discovery?",
    "category": "9. Microservices",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "In a microservices cloud environment, servers scale up and down dynamically, meaning their IP addresses change constantly. You cannot hardcode IP addresses.\n**Service Discovery** acts like a dynamic phone book. When a new service boots up, it registers its IP address with a central registry (like Netflix Eureka or Consul). When Service A needs to call Service B, it asks the registry: \"What is the current IP of Service B?\" The registry returns the IP, and Service A makes the call.",
