    "explanation": "Inter-service communication is how different microservices talk to each other to fulfill a business process. There are two primary paradigms:\n1. **Synchronous (HTTP/REST or gRPC):** Service A sends a request to Service B and waits (blocks) until Service B replies. \n2. **Asynchronous (Messaging via Kafka/RabbitMQ):** Service A publishes a message/event to a broker (\"User Created\") and immediately continues its work. Service B consumes that message whenever it is ready.",
