    "id": 147,
    "title": "What is authentication vs authorization?",
    "category": "10. Spring Security",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "- **Authentication:** \"Who are you?\" It is the process of verifying a user's identity (e.g., checking a username/password, or validating a JWT signature). If it fails, the server returns `401 Unauthorized`.\n- **Authorization:** \"Are you allowed to do this?\" Once identified, it is the process of verifying if the user has the required permissions or roles to access a specific resource. If it fails, the server returns `403 Forbidden`.",
    "example": "Authentication is showing your ID to the security guard to enter an office building. Authorization is whether that ID card actually unlocks the door to the CEO's office.",
