    "explanation": "CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery) is an attack where a malicious website tricks a user's web browser into performing an unwanted action on a trusted site where the user is currently authenticated.\nIf your API uses session cookies (`JSESSIONID`), the browser automatically attaches those cookies to *any* request made to your domain, even if the request was secretly triggered by a button on `hacker.com`.",
