    "title": "What is BCrypt?",
    "category": "10. Spring Security",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "BCrypt is a highly secure password hashing function. It is the default and recommended password encoder in Spring Security.\nUnlike simple hashing algorithms (like MD5 or SHA-256), BCrypt incorporates two critical security features:\n1. **Salting:** It automatically generates a random string (salt) and adds it to the password before hashing, defeating rainbow table attacks.\n2. **Work Factor:** It is intentionally designed to be slow. You can configure how many rounds of hashing it does. If hardware gets faster, you increase the work factor, ensuring it always takes ~250ms to hash a password, preventing brute-force attacks.",
