    "explanation": "To fully secure a production REST API:\n1. **HTTPS Only:** Enforce TLS/SSL at the infrastructure level (Gateway or Load Balancer).\n2. **Stateless Authentication:** Disable session creation in Spring Security. Use JWTs or OAuth2 Access Tokens.\n3. **CORS Configuration:** Strictly define allowed origins; never use `*`.\n4. **CSRF:** Disable it *only* if you are fully stateless (no cookies). Otherwise, implement CSRF tokens.\n5. **Role-Based Authorization:** Use `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole('ADMIN')\")` to protect sensitive endpoints.\n6. **Input Validation:** Use `@Valid` to prevent malicious payloads.\n7. **Rate Limiting:** Implement API rate limiting to prevent brute force and DDoS attacks.",
