    "category": "11. Caching & Performance",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Caching is a performance optimization technique where frequently requested data is temporarily stored in an ultra-fast storage layer (usually RAM).\nInstead of hitting the slow database or performing a complex, CPU-heavy calculation every single time a request comes in, the application checks the cache. If the data is there (Cache Hit), it returns it instantly. If not (Cache Miss), it fetches it from the database, saves a copy in the cache, and then returns it.",
