    "explanation": "Spring Boot provides a powerful, abstraction-based caching framework using annotations.\n1. Add the `@EnableCaching` annotation to your main application class.\n2. Annotate methods with `@Cacheable(\"cacheName\")`. Spring intercepts the method call. If the result is in the cache, it returns it instantly. If not, it executes the method and caches the result.\n3. Use `@CacheEvict` to remove data from the cache when the database is updated.\n4. Use `@CachePut` to update the cache without interfering with the method execution.",
