    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Opening a new physical connection to a database over the network is an extremely slow, CPU-intensive process (TCP handshake, authentication, memory allocation). \nConnection Pooling solves this by pre-creating a \"pool\" of ready-to-use database connections when the application starts.\nWhen a thread needs to execute SQL, it borrows a connection from the pool. When finished, it doesn't close the connection; it returns it to the pool for the next thread to use.",
