    "category": "11. Caching & Performance",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Although Java has automatic Garbage Collection, memory leaks can still occur.\nA memory leak happens when your application creates objects and maintains strong references to them long after they are no longer needed. Because the objects are still referenced by active code (e.g., stored in a static `HashMap`), the Garbage Collector cannot delete them.\nOver time, these useless objects consume the entire Heap memory, resulting in a fatal `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError`.",
