    "tip": "While H2 tries to emulate MySQL/PostgreSQL dialects, it is not perfect. This is why the industry is shifting towards TestContainers for true parity with production.",
    "mistake": "Accidentally deploying an application to production using an H2 database. As soon as the server restarts, all user data is permanently lost.",
    "summary": "A volatile, blazing-fast database that stores data in RAM, commonly used to execute database integration tests quickly."
