    "title": "What is Code Coverage?",
    "category": "12. Testing Backend Applications",
    "language": "java",
    "explanation": "Code coverage is a metric that measures the percentage of your application's source code that is executed when the automated test suite runs.\nIf you have 100 lines of code, and your tests only execute 80 of those lines, your code coverage is 80%. It specifically tracks branches (if/else statements) to ensure both true and false paths are tested.",
    "example": "If you have an `if (user == null)` block, but you never write a test that passes a null user, your code coverage tool will flag that block in red as \"untested code.\"",
